    "title": "Loaded Firearm Magazine Discovered on Frontier Flight at Hartsfield Jackson International Airport - NewsBreak",
    "text": "4 hours ago On November 9, 2025, airport staff found a loaded firearm magazine near seat 7A on a Frontier Airlines Airbus A320 at Hartsfield Jackson International Airport in Atlanta. The magazine contained ten hollow point rounds and was labeled 'K H.' The discovery happened during boarding for a flight to Cincinnati at Gate C-6.\nAirport officers, TSA, Homeland Security, and Atlanta Police K-9 units responded. They removed passengers from the plane and searched the aircraft. No other suspicious items were found. All passengers were screened again.\nThe flight left safely later that evening. The FBI was informed, and the investigation is ongoing.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
